                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            %p
              Abstract coordinate systems according to prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianSpacesAndSmoothFunctions"}
              form a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+Categories+and+Toposes#Categories"}> this def.
              ) – to be denoted
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              – whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are the abstract coordinate systems
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n}
                  (the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                  of objects is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \mathbb{R}^{n_1} \to \mathbb{R}^{n_2}
                  are the abstract
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+transformations"} coordinate transformations
                  \=
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            %p
              Composition of morphisms is given by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
